2. Scope of reference
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The MoonBit sources in this repository are a port of, and are derived from,
jlaffaye/ftp. The following upstream artifacts were used as the reference
basis:

- ftp.go, parse.go, status.go, scanner.go, walker.go, debug.go (implementation)
  and the matching *_test.go files (test cases and expectations), as mapped
  file-by-file in docs/porting/02-upstream-map.md.
- The LIST / MLSD line parsers and the "half-year rule" for timestamps in
  parse.go are behavior ports; the FTP response status table in status.go is
  ported into status.mbt.
- Test expectations were adapted from the upstream test suite. End-to-end
  tests run against a real server and are declared in ftp_server_test.mbt.

The port is not a mechanical translation: files were reorganized by
responsibility, the async I/O layer was rebuilt on `moonbitlang/async`, and
Go-specific types, error values and concurrency constraints were rewritten
using MoonBit idioms. The deliberate behavioral differences from the upstream
Go implementation are enumerated in docs/porting/02-upstream-map.md and
docs/porting/06-compat-checklist.md.

Per-file provenance: every file carrying ported code starts with a header of
the form

    // Ported from jlaffaye/ftp (ISC License), see LICENSE-THIRD-PARTY.

so the ISC terms above apply to those files.

